// Conformance: recovers a regression test for a real, already-fixed bug
// whose repro file was referenced by a source comment but never actually
// committed -- found while auditing LEDGER item 2c (commit e7b1599,
// "showcase: secret_agent password manager + fix assert_eq unwind-skip
// bug", cites `tests/known_failures/assert_eq_shadow_unwind_skip.kry` in a
// doc comment on `is_unwind_source` in kryos-mir/src/lower.rs, but that
// file does not exist in the tree and was never added in that commit or
// any other -- a slip, not an unfiled bug: the FIX itself (the
// `true_assert_eq_intrinsic` arity guard, present in both codegen backends
// and kryos-mir at this HEAD) was real and already shipped).
//
// The bug: `is_unwind_source`/the matching codegen post-call safety net
// excluded ANY call literally named `assert_eq` from the "may throw, check
// for a pending exception right after this call" treatment, regardless of
// arg count. That is correct for the TRUE 2-arg `assert_eq` intrinsic
// (which lowers to `kryos_builtin_assert_eq` and aborts the process
// directly -- it never returns, so no post-call check is needed or
// possible). It is WRONG for `std::test`'s 3-arg
// `assert_eq(actual, expected, msg)` (or any user function reusing the
// name), which is an ordinary function that can `throw` and return
// normally: the caller kept executing the statement(s) immediately after a
// failing 3-arg assert_eq -- even past the point a `try` should have
// unwound to its `catch` -- until some LATER, correctly-checked call site
// happened to notice the still-pending exception.
//
// Fix (already present, re-verified this session): the exclusion is now
// gated on `func == "assert_eq" && args.len() == 2` -- the true intrinsic's
// own arity -- in kryos-mir/src/lower.rs::is_unwind_source and the mirrored
// post-call check in both kryos-codegen-llvm and kryos-codegen-cranelift.
//
// Proof this is a real gate: reverting the `!args.is_empty()`/arg-count
// guard back to an unconditional `func == "assert_eq"` exclusion in all
// three sites makes `ran` below end up `11` (both statements after the
// failing assert_eq execute before the throw is noticed) instead of `0`;
// with the fix, `ran` stays `0` -- the exception unwinds at the assert_eq
// call site itself, on both backends.

use std::test::{assert_eq}

fn expect(cond: bool, what: str) {
    if not cond {
        println("CONF FAIL: {what}")
        exit(1)
    }
}

fn main() {
    // The failing call is nested one level INSIDE the try body (an `if`),
    // not at the try body's own top level: `lower_try_catch` already emits
    // an unconditional per-STATEMENT check for the try body's top level
    // (a separate, older mechanism), which would mask this bug for a
    // top-level call. `is_unwind_source`'s arity guard is what extends
    // exception detection to a call nested inside if/for/while/match
    // bodies within a try (see the doc comment on `emit()` in
    // kryos-mir/src/lower.rs) -- so the repro must be nested to actually
    // exercise the fixed code path.
    let mut ran: i64 = 0
    try {
        if true {
            assert_eq(2, 3, "deliberate mismatch")
            ran = ran + 1
            ran = ran + 10
        }
    } catch (e) {
        // Deliberately does NOT touch `ran` -- so a value other than 0
        // proves a statement after the failing call executed, not just
        // that the catch eventually ran.
        expect(contains(e, "deliberate mismatch"), "caught message should name the mismatch, got: " + e)
    }
    expect(ran == 0, "a failing 3-arg assert_eq must unwind IMMEDIATELY at its own call site, not defer to a later checked call; ran=" + to_string(ran))

    println("conformance assert_eq_unwind_immediate: PASS")
}
